/* WHERE REVERIE, LACE AND THE STREET CAT MAY BE PLACED (pure data and rules: browser and Node tests, and the server's copy through the admin inventory; no DOM, no network).
   The owner, 19 Nov 2026: "Let me place REVERIE or LACE anywhere": anywhere walkable in the city, not only the Avenue's north pavement. THE AREAS (one is built at a time
   in the game; a placement, a time block or a route is in ONE of them):
     avenue     The Avenue                     both pavements between the Function Gate and the East Gate, and the North Gate's walkers' doors
     oldtown    Old Town                       Main Street's pavements, the District alley, the access road's pavements, the way to Port Customs
     far-south  Far South                      Main Street's second stretch (pavements), the Far South Gate's walkers' door
     outskirts  The Outskirts                  the gravel walkways between the container homes
     port       The Port                       the landing pad and the walkers' side of the passage
     district   The Darknet District (inside)  the hallway (the entry inside the inner door), the store's customer side, the vending alcove (never the Sleeping Pod room: the player's own pod)
   THE CONTENT RULE (the owner's, never relaxed): never Milked (the building: inside its doors), never NULL (the club), never the District bar, the VR
   play area or the arcade room, never the Corporate District or the Temple (not city). Also blocked: roads (the taxis' lanes), the gates' insides, building interiors
   players cannot walk, walls and furniture.
   PUBLIC PAVEMENTS IN FRONT OF A VENUE (the owner, 20 Nov 2026: "but the sidewalk isn't inside the location. can you change this rule for places on sidewalks"): Main
   Street's pavement at NULL's door and in front of Milked's side street and service alley is ordinary public pavement: walked along and passed by everyone (routes,
   escorts, the crosswalks). Only a venue's DOORWAY (within about 1.5 m of its street door: `doorway:true`) stays a place nobody is put or waits in: check() refuses it
   for a spot, check(p, prefer, m, {passing:true}) and leg() let a walk pass over it.
   MILKED'S LANES (the owner, 20 Nov 2026: "I might add gameplay there or add areas"): its side street and its service alley are ordinary walkable ground for everyone
   (spots, routes, waits, escorts); only the doorways of Milked's front door (in the side street) and rear door (in the service alley) are never stood in, as NULL's.
   WHERE THE DATA COMES FROM: the walkable rectangles below are the game's own street and room geometry (neochinatown.js streets and pavements, ncz-quarters.js gates
   and taxi posts, milked.js, ncz-nightclub.js, the District's local plan); OBSTACLES and the ground height (GEN) were read from the built scenes by
   tests/npc-obstacles-browser.cjs (street furniture by rays, plus the game's own collision solids from neochinatown.js layout()): rerun it when a street or room changes.
   ADULT VENUES (the owner, 19 Nov 2026: characters made with the Mission giver creator and marked "adult (18+)" may also stand in Milked's doorways and
   reception, NULL (inside and in its doorway), the District bar, the VR play area, the arcade room and the smoking terrace): those forbidden rectangles carry `adult:true` and
   walkable ground for them is listed with `adult:true` (only an adult made character ever uses it; check(p, prefer, m, {adult:true}) skips the adult rules). Never relaxed for
   anyone: Reverie, Lace and the cat, the Milked studios and staff rooms, the Sleeping Pod room, the Corporate District, the Temple. The inside of Milked is its own scene
   (area `milked`: its reception only). NULL's floor keeps clear of its furniture (ncz-nightclub.js solids); the District's rooms are open floor with their furniture unmapped.
   BACK ALLEYS, BAYS AND YARDS (the owner, 20 Nov 2026; ncz-backalleys.js): the narrow alleys behind the housing in The Avenue, Old Town and Far South, their loading bays and
   yards are ordinary walkable ground for everyone placed or routed here (spots, routes, waits, escorts); their furniture (dumpsters, crates, docks) and the ground under each
   fire escape are obstacles. The street crowd never goes in (it keeps to its pavement lanes, ncz-nightlife.js).
   check(p, prefer, m, opts {adult, made, passing}) -> {ok, area, kind, why}; leg(a, b, opts) -> problems; nearest(p, area, limit, opts) -> a spot she may stand on; areaOf(p); placeOf(...). */
